{"id":"a627a5785ab31788","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-simple-algebra.md","title":"Simple Algebra","display":"df-simple-algebra — Simple Algebra","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-simple-algebra","aliases":["58-df-simple-algebra","Simple Algebra"],"display":"df-simple-algebra — Simple Algebra","depends_on":["[[58-df-algebra]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-simple-algebra"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-simple-algebra</span><span>Simple Algebra</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-simple-algebra — Simple Algebra"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"573b416d39297a97\" href=\"?note=573b416d39297a97\" title=\"58-df-algebra\">58-df-algebra</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A\\in V\">\\(k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A\\in V\\)</span> (base field, algebra carrier, operations, and additive zero)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Alg}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Alg}_S\\)</span> (algebra predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"573b416d39297a97\" href=\"?note=573b416d39297a97\" title=\"58-df-algebra\">58-df-algebra</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\">\\(\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\)</span> (expanded below rather than imported from the unrelated generic ideal atom)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S\\)</span> (simple-algebra predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}two\\text{-}sided\\text{-}ideal}\\vdash\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\leftrightarrow I\\subseteq A\\land0_A\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay\\in I)\\land\\forall x\\in I\\;\\exists y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay=0_A)\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(a\\cdot_Ax\\in I\\land x\\cdot_Aa\\in I)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}two\\text{-}sided\\text{-}ideal}\\vdash\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\leftrightarrow I\\subseteq A\\land0_A\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay\\in I)\\land\\forall x\\in I\\;\\exists y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay=0_A)\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(a\\cdot_Ax\\in I\\land x\\cdot_Aa\\in I)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}algebra} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S(A,k,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Alg}_S(k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A)\\land 0_A\\in A\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;(0_A+_Aa=a=a+_A0_A)\\land A\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land\\neg\\exists I\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\land I\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land I\\neq A\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}algebra} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S(A,k,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Alg}_S(k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A)\\land 0_A\\in A\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;(0_A+_Aa=a=a+_A0_A)\\land A\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land\\neg\\exists I\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\land I\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land I\\neq A\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A simple algebra is nonzero and has no nontrivial two-sided ideals.</li>\n<li>Additive closure and additive inverses are expanded using only the supplied operation and zero; no undeclared unary-negation operation remains.</li>\n<li>Wedderburn consequences, centrality, tensor products, and the Brauer group are downstream atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Herstein, Noncommutative Rings</li>\n<li>Lam, First Course in Noncommutative Rings</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"573b416d39297a97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-algebra]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"573b416d39297a97","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Alg}_S$ (algebra predicate, see [[58-df-algebra]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Alg}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}two\\text{-}sided\\text{-}ideal}\\vdash\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\leftrightarrow I\\subseteq A\\land0_A\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay\\in I)\\land\\forall x\\in I\\;\\exists y\\in I\\;(x+_Ay=0_A)\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(a\\cdot_Ax\\in I\\land x\\cdot_Aa\\in I)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}algebra} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S(A,k,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Alg}_S(k,A,+_A,\\cdot_A)\\land 0_A\\in A\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;(0_A+_Aa=a=a+_A0_A)\\land A\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land\\neg\\exists I\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{TwoSidedIdeal}_{A,+_A,\\cdot_A,0_A}(I)\\land I\\neq\\{0_A\\}\\land I\\neq A\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1753,"backlinks":[{"id":"10d54928fc77535a","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SimpleAlgebra}_S$ (simple-algebra predicate, see [[58-df-simple-algebra]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1167","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-simple-algebra.md|58-df-simple-algebra]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["573b416d39297a97"]}